```markdown
# Architecture

## Overview

LLM-Train is a 1-trillion parameter language model training system written in Zig with CUDA kernels, targeting NVIDIA B200 GPUs (SM 100 architecture).

## Model Architecture

The model uses a hybrid recurrent-associative architecture combining two novel memory mechanisms per layer:

### EFLA (Exponential Fast Linear Attention)

EFLA replaces standard self-attention with a linear recurrent update rule. At each time step t, a matrix state H is maintained per head:

H_t = H_{t-1} + beta * lambda_t * (v_t - H_{t-1} k_t) outer k_t

where lambda_t = 1 / (1 + beta * k_t^T H_{t-1} k_t) is a dynamic gating scalar. This achieves O(L) complexity in sequence length with O(d^2) state per head.

### PRISM (Progressive Recurrent Iterative State Machine)

PRISM applies a short depthwise convolution followed by multi-iteration rank-1 state updates:

S_t = alpha * S_{t-1} + sum_l beta_l * delta_l outer k_l

where beta_l, k_l, delta_l are linear projections of the convolution output. The state S is a hidden_dim x hidden_dim matrix.

### FFN

Each block uses a standard SwiGLU-style FFN with GELU activation:

ffn(x) = down(gelu(up(x)))

### Layer Structure

Each block applies: RMSNorm -> EFLA -> residual -> RMSNorm -> PRISM -> residual -> RMSNorm -> FFN -> residual

### Tied Embeddings

Input and output embeddings share weights, reducing parameter count significantly.

## Optimizer

Embedding and FFN weights use Lion (sign-based momentum). Attention and recurrent weights use Muon (Newton-Schulz orthogonalization before SGD with momentum). Both use cosine LR scheduling with linear warmup.

## Parallelism

Tensor parallelism splits attention heads and FFN columns across GPUs. ZeRO-3 shards optimizer state, gradients, and parameters across all ranks. NCCL Ring AllReduce is used for gradient synchronization.

## Precision

FP8 E4M3 for forward pass activations and weights with MX block scaling (block size 32). FP32 master weights and optimizer states.

## Checkpointing

Binary per-tensor files with SHA-256 manifest for integrity verification. Supports mid-epoch resume via token position tracking.
